dict(pas="17.1", w="陽貨=yáng huò/Yang Huo//Yang (surname)//Huo (his name) | 欲/wanted | 見=jiàn/to see | 孔子；=kǒng zǐ/Kongzi | ^孔子=kǒng zǐ/Kongzi | 不/would not | 見。=jiàn/see (him) | ^歸=guī/(Yang Huo) sent as a gift | 孔子=kǒng zǐ/(to) Kongzi | 豚。=tún/a young pig | ^孔子=kǒng zǐ/Kongzi | 時/timed it | 其/(for) his | 亡=wú/being out | 也/(pause) | 而/and | 往/went | 拜/to bow (his thanks) | 之；/to him | ^遇=yù/(and) met | 諸=zhū/him on (= 之於) | 塗。=tú/the road",
  l="Yang Huo wanted to see Kongzi;\nKongzi would not see him.\nHe sent Kongzi a young pig.\nKongzi, timing it for when he was out, went to bow his thanks to him;\nhe met him on the road.",
  i="Yang Huo wanted Kongzi to call on him, and Kongzi would not go. So Yang Huo had a young pig delivered to him. Kongzi picked a moment when Yang Huo was away from home and went to bow his thanks at his door — and ran into him on the road.",
  n="The book is named 陽貨 from its opening words; Zhu Xi counts twenty-six chapters (凡二十六章), and our numbers are his. 陽貨 Yang Huo, Zhu Xi says, was a retainer of the Ji house named Hu (陽貨季氏家臣名虎) — that is, Yang Hu, whom you met at 9.5, 16.2 and 16.3; he had once imprisoned Ji Huanzi and taken the government of the state into his own hands (嘗囚季桓子而專國政). He Yan's Kong Anguo agrees (陽貨陽虎也): a retainer of the Ji who ran the government of Lu and wanted to see Kongzi to make him take office. 見 jiàn 'to see' — Zhu Xi: he wanted to make Kongzi come and see him (欲令孔子來見己), and Kongzi would not go. 歸 here is 'to send as a gift'. Zhu Xi notes 歸如字一作饋: read it as written, guī, though one text writes 饋 'to present food' (those who follow 饋 read kuì). 豚 tún is a young pig. Zhu Xi explains the move: by the rites, when a grandee sent a gift to an officer and the officer could not receive it at his own house, he went and bowed at the grandee's gate (禮大夫有賜於士不得受於其家則往拜其門); so Huo watched for Kongzi to be out (瞰孔子之亡) and sent the pig, to make Kongzi come and bow and so meet him. 亡 is read wú, 'not there, away' (= 無). 時 is a verb here, 'to time it, to wait for the moment'. 諸 is the fused 之於 'him at': 遇諸塗 'met him on the road' (Kong Anguo: 塗道也). Zhu Xi weighs each step: not going to see him was what was right (義); going to bow was the rites (禮); choosing the time of his absence was to answer him in kind (欲其稱也); not avoiding him on the road was not cutting him off for ever (不終絶也)."),
dict(w="謂/(Yang Huo) spoke to | 孔子=kǒng zǐ/Kongzi | 曰：「/saying | 來！/come | 予=yú/I | 與=yǔ/with | 爾/you | 言。」/will talk | ^曰：「/(he) said | 懷=huái/to hold in one's bosom | 其/one's | 寶=bǎo/treasure | 而/and yet | 迷=mí/to leave astray | 其/one's | 邦，/state | 可/can (it) | 謂/be called | 仁/humane | 乎？」/(question) | ^曰：「/(Kongzi) said | 不/(it) cannot | 可。」「/(be) | ^好=hào/to be fond of | 從=cóng/taking part in | 事/affairs | 而/and yet | 亟=qì/again and again | 失/to miss | 時，/the moment | 可/can (it) | 謂/be called | 知=zhì/wise | 乎？」/(question) | ^曰：「/(Kongzi) said | 不/(it) cannot | 可。」「/(be) | ^日/the days | 月/(and) months | 逝=shì/go by | 矣，/(so it is) | 嵗=suì/the years | 不/do not | 我/(for) us | 與。」=yǔ/stay | ^孔子=kǒng zǐ/Kongzi | 曰：「/said | 諾，/very well | 吾/I | 將=jiāng/am going to | 仕/take office | 矣。」/(so it is)",
  l="He said to Kongzi: “Come! I will talk with you.”\nHe said: “Holding one's treasure in one's bosom and leaving one's state astray — can that be called humane?”\nHe said: “It cannot.”\n“Fond of taking part in affairs, and yet again and again missing the moment — can that be called wise?”\nHe said: “It cannot.”\n“The days and months go by; the years do not stay for us.”\nKongzi said: “Very well. I am going to take office.”",
  i="He called out to Kongzi, “Come here, I have something to say to you. To hide away your treasure while your state goes astray — would you call that humane?” “No,” said Kongzi. “To long for a part in affairs and yet let the moment slip by time after time — would you call that wise?” “No.” “The days and months are slipping past, and the years will not linger for you.” “Very well,” said Kongzi. “In time I shall take office.”",
  n="予 yú 'I'; 與 yǔ 'with'. 懷 is to hold in the bosom, to keep tucked away (15.6 可巻而懷之), 寶 bǎo a treasure, and 迷 mí 'lost, astray', here a verb with an object: to leave one's state in confusion. Zhu Xi: keeping the Way and virtue hidden and not saving the state from its confusion (懷寶迷邦謂懷藏道徳不救國之迷亂); He Yan's Ma Rong: not taking office is hiding the treasure, and knowing the state is ill governed yet not governing it is leaving it astray. 好 hào 'fond of'; 從事 'to take part in affairs'. 亟 qì 'often' (Zhu Xi: 亟數也), and 失時 is failing to be in time for the moment when things can be turned (失時謂不及事幾之㑹). 知 is zhì 'wise'. Zhu Xi marks 好亟知並去聲, all three as modern Mandarin reads them. He Yan's text writes 智 for 知 'wise', here and at 17.3 — the same word. 逝 shì 'to go by'; 嵗 is the edition's form of 歲 suì 'year'. 不我與 'not us stay-with': after a negative, a pronoun object comes before the verb (as 不己知, 1.16); 與 yǔ is to keep company with, to wait for. The text never names who answers 曰不可. Zhu Xi takes the answers as Kongzi's — he answered each question as it came because right was on his side (隨問而對者理之直也), and answered without arguing, his words yielding yet giving nothing away (對而不辯者言之孫而亦無所詘也). Huo's words, he says, all mocked Kongzi and hinted that he should take office quickly (貨語皆譏孔子而諷使速仕); Kongzi had never been as Huo described, nor was he unwilling to serve — only not under Huo (但不仕於貨耳), so he answered straight from principle as if he had missed the hint (若不諭其意者). 將 jiāng 'am going to': Zhu Xi, a word for what is about to be but is not yet certain (將者且然而未必之辭). Kong Anguo: with compliant words he kept out of harm. Zhu Xi adds that Huo's wish to see him, however kindly put, was only to get his help in disorder. He ends with Yang Shi: Yang Xiong said that with Yang Huo Kongzi 'paid respect where none was due, bending his person to make the Way prevail' (敬所不敬為詘身以信道) — a man who says this does not know Kongzi: there is no self outside the Way and no Way outside the self; bend the self, and can the Way be made to prevail? 'I do not believe it.'"),
